{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Blocked on design (no code changed, not claimed): the MCP op-cert signer reads the same setting as authorship. src/rebar/mcp_server.py compose_startup_opcert_binding() builds the startup op-cert signer from cfg.identity.signing_key (REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY) plus REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID, and main() binds it for every certified tool. Pointing REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY at /run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key would make plan-review and completion-verifier certs sign with the bot key under env 9f1c8e42-..., which is not in REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS. tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py (around line 152) pins that coupling. Separating the two keys needs a code change to the op-cert key source (e.g. read REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH, which the opcert service already uses), awaiting operator decision."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795140503854703001,"uuid":"a73198f3-c1d8-4ecc-9def-8df24121e5f0"}